cf-feat-animal-companion-ranger = Animal Companion (Ranger)
cf-feat-animal-companion-ranger-desc = You gain an animal companion. Pick it on the Pet tab.
cf-feat-animal-empathy = Animal Empathy
cf-feat-animal-empathy-desc = Speak to animals: TBA
cf-feat-animal-empathy-ranger = Animal Empathy (Ranger)
cf-feat-animal-empathy-ranger-desc = Speak to animals: TBA
cf-feat-anoint-ally = Anoint Ally
cf-feat-anoint-ally-desc = Costs 1 action. Blood magic is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-antagonize = Antagonize
cf-feat-antagonize-desc = A Demoralized creature stays frightened until it attacks you: TBA
cf-feat-anthropomorphic-shape = Anthropomorphic Shape
cf-feat-anthropomorphic-shape-desc = Requires Untamed Form. Untamed Form can make you look like a humanoid. Disguises are not in the game: TBA
cf-feat-apparition-sense = Apparition Sense
cf-feat-apparition-sense-desc = Sense spirits and undead. This one: TBA
cf-feat-apparitions-enhancement = Apparition's Enhancement
cf-feat-apparitions-enhancement-desc = Free action, automatic. After you cast a spell that is not a cantrip, your next Strike that hits within 6 seconds deals 1d6 spirit damage more.
cf-feat-arcane-evolution = Arcane Evolution
cf-feat-arcane-evolution-desc = Requires a bloodline with arcane spells. You are trained in one skill of your choice. Each day, one spell you know is a signature spell: change it on the character sheet's Daily tab, and it takes over at your next long rest. Adding spells with Learn a Spell: TBA
cf-feat-arcane-fists = Arcane Fists
cf-feat-arcane-fists-desc = Your fist deals 1d6 and is lethal.
cf-feat-area-armor = Area Armor
cf-feat-area-armor-desc = Adjacent allies get a bonus to Reflex against areas: TBA
cf-feat-armored-courage = Armored Courage
cf-feat-armored-courage-desc = Costs 1 action, once an hour, in medium or heavy armor. Temporary Hit Points equal to your level for a minute, and frightened goes down by 1.
cf-feat-armored-regiment-training = Armored Regiment Training
cf-feat-armored-regiment-training-desc = Armor training for a regiment: TBA
cf-feat-artists-attendance = Artist's Attendance
cf-feat-artists-attendance-desc = Costs 2 actions. This one: TBA
cf-feat-assisting-shot = Assisting Shot
cf-feat-assisting-shot-desc = Costs 1 action. A shot that helps the next attack on a foe: TBA
cf-feat-astral-tether = Astral Tether
cf-feat-astral-tether-desc = Costs 1 action. Share an amp with an ally. Amps from feats are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-athletic-strategist = Athletic Strategist
cf-feat-athletic-strategist-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. Use a stored roll for a maneuver: TBA
cf-feat-auraof-courage = Aura of Courage
cf-feat-auraof-courage-desc = Requires a holy cause. When you become frightened, the value is 1 lower, and every 6 seconds allies in your aura lose 1 from frightened.
cf-feat-auraof-despair = Aura of Despair
cf-feat-auraof-despair-desc = Requires an unholy cause. Enemies in your aura take -1 circumstance to saves against fear, and their frightened does not ease below 1 while they stay.
cf-feat-backup-runic-enhancement = Backup Runic Enhancement
cf-feat-backup-runic-enhancement-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-banner-twirl = Banner Twirl
cf-feat-banner-twirl-desc = Costs 1 action. A use of your banner: TBA
cf-feat-banners-inspiration = Banner's Inspiration
cf-feat-banners-inspiration-desc = Costs 1 action. Everyone in your squad loses 1 from frightened. The new save: TBA
cf-feat-bardic-lore = Bardic Lore
cf-feat-bardic-lore-desc = Requires enigma muse. Lore: Bardic Lore.
cf-feat-barreling-charge-barbarian = Barreling Charge
cf-feat-barreling-charge-barbarian-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. Costs 2 actions. You rush up to 25 feet to an enemy and Strike it. Creatures do not block each other here, so there is no Athletics check to get past those in the way.
cf-feat-barreling-charge-fighter = Barreling Charge
cf-feat-barreling-charge-fighter-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. Costs 2 actions. You rush up to 25 feet to an enemy and Strike it. Creatures do not block each other here, so there is no Athletics check to get past those in the way.
cf-feat-bashing-charge = Bashing Charge
cf-feat-bashing-charge-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. Costs 2 actions. Stride twice and Force Open a door or wall on the way. It needs a path to follow: TBA
cf-feat-basic-lesson = Basic Lesson
cf-feat-basic-lesson-desc = Choose a lesson. Life: the life boost hex. Protection: the blood ward hex. Dreams: the veil of dreams hex. Each hex costs a Focus Point, and adds one to your pool. The lessons of the Elements and of Vengeance, and the spell your familiar learns: TBA
cf-feat-bespell-strikes-oracle = Bespell Strikes
cf-feat-bespell-strikes-oracle-desc = Free action, automatic. After you cast a spell that is not a cantrip, your next Strike that hits within 6 seconds deals 1d6 force damage more. Taking the spell's own damage type: TBA
cf-feat-bespell-strikes-sorcerer = Bespell Strikes
cf-feat-bespell-strikes-sorcerer-desc = Free action, automatic. After you cast a spell that is not a cantrip, your next Strike that hits within 6 seconds deals 1d6 force damage more. Taking the spell's own damage type: TBA
cf-feat-bespell-strikes-wizard = Bespell Strikes
cf-feat-bespell-strikes-wizard-desc = Free action, automatic. After you cast a spell that is not a cantrip, your next Strike that hits within 6 seconds deals 1d6 force damage more. Taking the spell's own damage type: TBA
cf-feat-bestial-snarling = Bestial Snarling
cf-feat-bestial-snarling-desc = Requires zoophonia muse. Costs 1 action. Frighten adjacent enemies with a growl: TBA
cf-feat-black-powder-boost = Black Powder Boost
cf-feat-black-powder-boost-desc = Costs 1 or 2 actions. Fire your gun to jump further. There are no High Jump or Long Jump actions to add the distance to: TBA
cf-feat-blade-brake = Blade Brake
cf-feat-blade-brake-desc = Reaction. Anchor yourself against forced movement. There is no trigger for it yet: TBA
cf-feat-blast-lock = Blast Lock
cf-feat-blast-lock-desc = Costs 1 action. Shoot a lock open. TBA
cf-feat-bleed-out = Bleed Out
cf-feat-bleed-out-desc = Costs 1 action, within 6 seconds of your blood magic. A spell attack against a creature within 60 feet: on a hit it takes persistent bleed damage equal to the rank of the spell that set the blood magic off.
cf-feat-blood-rising = Blood Rising
cf-feat-blood-rising-desc = Reaction. Blood magic is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-bloodletting-claws = Bloodletting Claws
cf-feat-bloodletting-claws-desc = Your eidolon causes bleeding. This one: TBA
cf-feat-blowgun-poisoner = Blowgun Poisoner
cf-feat-blowgun-poisoner-desc = Poison with a blowgun. Injury poisons are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-body-shield = Body Shield
