cf-feat-bodyguard = Bodyguard
cf-feat-bodyguard-desc = Swear to protect one ally, for a bigger Taunt penalty against them. Choosing that ally: TBA
cf-feat-bone-speaker = Bone Speaker
cf-feat-bone-speaker-desc = Use Undead Lore on living skeletons. Undead Lore is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-bony-barrage = Bony Barrage
cf-feat-bony-barrage-desc = You learn Bony Barrage, a grave spell. Destroying a second thrall for armor: TBA
cf-feat-brandishing-draw = Brandishing Draw
cf-feat-brandishing-draw-desc = Costs 1 action. Draw a weapon and Strike with it: TBA
cf-feat-breached-defenses = Breached Defenses
cf-feat-breached-defenses-desc = Requires Exploit Vulnerability. Get past resistances: TBA
cf-feat-brilliant-flash = Brilliant Flash
cf-feat-brilliant-flash-desc = Requires grandeur cause. Flash of Grandeur also leaves the attacker off-guard for 6 seconds.
cf-feat-brutal-beating = Brutal Beating
cf-feat-brutal-beating-desc = Requires the ruffian racket. A critical hit that deals damage leaves the target frightened 1.
cf-feat-brutal-crush-barbarian = Brutal Crush
cf-feat-brutal-crush-barbarian-desc = Requires animal instinct. Costs 1 action. While raging with your animal attack, if it deals bludgeoning damage: an unarmed Strike at the creature you last attacked this turn. If it deals damage the target is stupefied 2 for 6 seconds, or 3 on a critical hit.
cf-feat-brutal-crush-druid = Brutal Crush
cf-feat-brutal-crush-druid-desc = Requires untamed order. Costs 1 action. In a battle form whose attack deals bludgeoning damage, such as the ape: an unarmed Strike at the creature you last attacked this turn. If it deals damage the target is stupefied 2 for 6 seconds, or 3 on a critical hit.
cf-feat-brutish-shove = Brutish Shove
cf-feat-brutish-shove-desc = Costs 1 action, after another attack this turn. A Strike with a two-handed weapon. A hit leaves the target off-guard for 6 seconds and shoves it 5 feet, 10 on a critical hit. A miss still leaves it off-guard. It works on a creature of any size.
cf-feat-built-in-tools = Built-In Tools
cf-feat-built-in-tools-desc = Tools built into your innovation. This option: TBA
cf-feat-bulletanda-broadside = Bullet and a Broadside
cf-feat-bulletanda-broadside-desc = Use a siege weapon. Siege weapons are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-burning-cascade = Burning Cascade
cf-feat-burning-cascade-desc = Requires Arcane Cascade. Fire around you when you enter the stance: TBA
cf-feat-cackle = Cackle
cf-feat-cackle-desc = One more Focus Point. The cackle hex sustains a spell for free: spells here sustain themselves, so it has nothing else to do.
cf-feat-call-implement = Call Implement
cf-feat-call-implement-desc = Costs 1 action. Your implement returns to your hand: TBA
cf-feat-call-wizardly-tools = Call Wizardly Tools
