cf-feat-channelers-stance = Channeler's Stance
cf-feat-channelers-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-charmed-life = Charmed Life
cf-feat-charmed-life-desc = Requires Charisma +2. Reaction, automatic. +2 circumstance to a saving throw, when that would improve the result. Gain panache if you succeed.
cf-feat-cheaters-always-prosper = Cheaters Always Prosper
cf-feat-cheaters-always-prosper-desc = Requires Dirty Trick. TBA
cf-feat-circleof-spirits = Circle of Spirits
cf-feat-circleof-spirits-desc = Costs 1 action, once per round. Your second apparition becomes your primary one.
cf-feat-clever-gambit = Clever Gambit
cf-feat-clever-gambit-desc = Requires mastermind racket. Reaction. Step after a critical hit on a foe you studied: TBA
cf-feat-clotting-elixirs = Clotting Elixirs
cf-feat-clotting-elixirs-desc = Your healing elixirs can stop bleeding: TBA
cf-feat-cobra-stance = Cobra Stance
cf-feat-cobra-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. Your only Strikes are 1d4 piercing cobra fangs (agile, deadly d10, finesse), and you have +1 circumstance to Fortitude saves. Poison resistance and the bonus to your Fortitude DC: TBA
cf-feat-collapse-armor = Collapse Armor
cf-feat-collapse-armor-desc = Requires armor innovation. Costs 1 action. This option: TBA
cf-feat-collapse-construct = Collapse Construct
cf-feat-collapse-construct-desc = Requires construct innovation. Costs 1 action. This option: TBA
cf-feat-combat-assessment-commander = Combat Assessment
cf-feat-combat-assessment-commander-desc = Costs 1 action. A melee Strike. If it hits, you also Recall Knowledge about the target at no extra cost. The +2 to that check on a critical hit: TBA
cf-feat-combat-assessment-fighter = Combat Assessment
cf-feat-combat-assessment-fighter-desc = Costs 1 action. A melee Strike. If it hits, you also Recall Knowledge about the target at no extra cost. The +2 to that check on a critical hit: TBA
cf-feat-combat-grab = Combat Grab
cf-feat-combat-grab-desc = Costs 1 action, after another attack this turn, with one hand free. A melee Strike that grabs the target if it hits, for 6 seconds or until it Escapes.
cf-feat-combat-reading = Combat Reading
cf-feat-combat-reading-desc = Costs 1 action. Learn a foe's strengths and weaknesses: TBA
cf-feat-commanders-companion = Commander's Companion
cf-feat-commanders-companion-desc = An animal companion for your banner: TBA
cf-feat-communal-healing = Communal Healing
cf-feat-communal-healing-desc = When your Heal restores Hit Points to one creature, another living creature within 30 feet regains Hit Points equal to the spell's rank: you if it was someone else, otherwise the nearest hurt ally.
cf-feat-companions-cry = Companion's Cry
cf-feat-companions-cry-desc = Requires an animal companion. TBA
cf-feat-conceal-spell-animist = Conceal Spell
cf-feat-conceal-spell-animist-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell does not set off reactions.
cf-feat-conceal-spell-necromancer = Conceal Spell
cf-feat-conceal-spell-necromancer-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell does not set off reactions.
cf-feat-conceal-spell-witch = Conceal Spell
cf-feat-conceal-spell-witch-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell does not set off reactions.
cf-feat-conceal-spell-wizard = Conceal Spell
cf-feat-conceal-spell-wizard-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell does not set off reactions.
cf-feat-convergent-tides = Convergent Tides
cf-feat-convergent-tides-desc = Requires Arcane Cascade. Ignore water terrain. Water is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-counter-thought = Counter Thought
cf-feat-counter-thought-desc = Reaction. When an enemy you can see within 60 feet casts a mental spell, you spend a spell slot of that spell's rank, or the next one you have left above it, and try to counteract it.
cf-feat-counterspell-prepared-witch = Counterspell (Prepared)
cf-feat-counterspell-prepared-witch-desc = Reaction, automatic. When an enemy you can see within 60 feet casts a spell you have prepared, spend that prepared spell to try to counteract it.
cf-feat-counterspell-prepared-wizard = Counterspell (Prepared)
cf-feat-counterspell-prepared-wizard-desc = Reaction, automatic. When an enemy you can see within 60 feet casts a spell you have prepared, spend that prepared spell to try to counteract it.
cf-feat-courageous-advance = Courageous Advance
cf-feat-courageous-advance-desc = Requires warrior muse. Costs 1 action. An ally Strides when you cast courageous anthem. Compositions are not spells yet: TBA
cf-feat-cover-fire = Cover Fire
cf-feat-cover-fire-desc = Costs 1 action. A shot that makes a foe duck: TBA
cf-feat-covering-stance = Covering Stance
cf-feat-covering-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. Give an adjacent ally cover: TBA
cf-feat-crane-stance = Crane Stance
cf-feat-crane-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. +1 circumstance bonus to AC. Your only Strikes are 1d6 bludgeoning crane wing attacks (agile, finesse, nonlethal). The easier jumps: TBA
cf-feat-creature-comforts-barbarian = Creature Comforts
cf-feat-creature-comforts-barbarian-desc = Requires animal instinct. Reaction. When you become frightened while raging with your animal attack, the frightened value is 1 lower.
cf-feat-creature-comforts-druid = Creature Comforts
cf-feat-creature-comforts-druid-desc = Requires untamed order. Reaction. When you become frightened while in a battle form, the frightened value is 1 lower.
cf-feat-crossbow-ace = Crossbow Ace
cf-feat-crossbow-ace-desc = Costs 1 action. Reload while diverting or taking cover: TBA
cf-feat-crossbow-crack-shot = Crossbow Crack Shot
cf-feat-crossbow-crack-shot-desc = Reloading your crossbow adds range and damage. Reloading is not a separate action here: TBA
cf-feat-cruelty = Cruelty
cf-feat-cruelty-desc = Requires Touch of the Void. You can cast it with 2 actions: on a failed save the target is also enfeebled 1 for a minute, or enfeebled 2 on a critical failure.
cf-feat-crushing-grab = Crushing Grab
cf-feat-crushing-grab-desc = A successful Grapple also deals your Strength modifier in bludgeoning damage.
cf-feat-cryptic-spell = Cryptic Spell
cf-feat-cryptic-spell-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell does not set off reactions. Needing natural terrain: TBA
cf-feat-dancing-leaf = Dancing Leaf
cf-feat-dancing-leaf-desc = Your Leap goes 5 feet further. Falling beside a wall: TBA
cf-feat-dastardly-dash = Dastardly Dash
cf-feat-dastardly-dash-desc = Costs 1 action. Run past a foe and trip it: TBA
cf-feat-deadly-simplicity = Deadly Simplicity
cf-feat-deadly-simplicity-desc = Requires deity with a simple or unarmed attack favored weapon and trained with your deity's favored weapon. Your deity's favored weapon deals damage with a die one step larger. It does nothing for a deity whose weapon is not simple.
cf-feat-death-speaker = Death Speaker
cf-feat-death-speaker-desc = Your magic works on mindless undead: TBA
cf-feat-deathly-scream = Deathly Scream
cf-feat-deathly-scream-desc = You learn Deathly Scream, a grave spell.
cf-feat-deceptive-tactics = Deceptive Tactics
cf-feat-deceptive-tactics-desc = Use Warfare Lore for Create a Diversion and Feint: TBA
cf-feat-defend-summoner = Defend Summoner
cf-feat-defend-summoner-desc = Costs 1 action. +2 circumstance to your AC for 6 seconds.
cf-feat-defensive-advance-champion = Defensive Advance
cf-feat-defensive-advance-champion-desc = Costs 2 actions. You raise your shield, rush up to 25 feet to an enemy and Strike it.
cf-feat-defensive-advance-guardian = Defensive Advance
cf-feat-defensive-advance-guardian-desc = Costs 2 actions. You raise your shield, rush up to 25 feet to an enemy and Strike it.
cf-feat-defensive-armaments = Defensive Armaments
cf-feat-defensive-armaments-desc = You gain the Defensive Armaments action: with a crossbow or firearm in both hands, +1 circumstance bonus to AC for 6 seconds, at 1 action. Immunity to splash damage while parrying: TBA
cf-feat-defensive-swap = Defensive Swap
cf-feat-defensive-swap-desc = Reaction. Swap places with an ally under attack. Reactions cannot move you yet: TBA
cf-feat-deflect-projectile = Deflect Projectile
cf-feat-deflect-projectile-desc = Reaction, automatic. +4 circumstance to AC against a ranged Strike, when that would change the result. You need a free hand, and cannot be off-guard to the attacker.
cf-feat-deitys-domain = Deity's Domain
cf-feat-deitys-domain-desc = Pick one of your deity's domains, and gain its domain spell and a Focus Point.
cf-feat-desperate-prayer = Desperate Prayer
cf-feat-desperate-prayer-desc = Free action, once a day. You regain 1 Focus Point. The rules give it only with none left and only for a devotion spell.
cf-feat-detectives-readiness = Detective's Readiness
cf-feat-detectives-readiness-desc = A bonus to saves on a case. Investigations do not exist: TBA
cf-feat-devastating-spellstrike = Devastating Spellstrike
cf-feat-devastating-spellstrike-desc = Requires inexorable iron hybrid study. Costs 2 actions. A Spellstrike that hits nearby foes: TBA
cf-feat-directed-audience = Directed Audience
cf-feat-directed-audience-desc = Change a composition's emanation to a cone. Compositions are not spells yet: TBA
cf-feat-directed-channel = Directed Channel
cf-feat-directed-channel-desc = Heal and Harm get a fourth choice on the wheel: 3 actions for a 60-foot cone aimed at the creature you click, in place of the 30-foot emanation.
cf-feat-disarming-flair = Disarming Flair
cf-feat-disarming-flair-desc = You gain panache from a successful Disarm, whatever your style.
cf-feat-disrupt-prey = Disrupt Prey
cf-feat-disrupt-prey-desc = Reaction, automatic. Strike your prey when it runs out of your reach. Disrupting its action on a critical hit: TBA
cf-feat-distant-waterbirds-poise = Distant Waterbird's Poise
cf-feat-distant-waterbirds-poise-desc = Requires aloof firmament hybrid study. Reaction. Leap away after a Spellstrike. Reactions cannot move you yet: TBA
cf-feat-distracting-feint = Distracting Feint
cf-feat-distracting-feint-desc = Requires scoundrel racket. While a creature is off-guard from your Feint, it also takes -2 circumstance to Perception and Reflex saves.
cf-feat-distracting-spellstrike = Distracting Spellstrike
cf-feat-distracting-spellstrike-desc = Requires laughing shadow hybrid study. Costs 2 actions. Spellstrike and Feint together: TBA
cf-feat-diverse-lore = Diverse Lore
cf-feat-diverse-lore-desc = Esoteric Lore about any topic: TBA
cf-feat-divert-streamflow = Divert Streamflow
cf-feat-divert-streamflow-desc = Reaction. Reposition an attacker and Step. Reactions cannot move you yet: TBA
cf-feat-divine-aegis = Divine Aegis
cf-feat-divine-aegis-desc = Reaction. A better save against other magic, and a worse one against divine magic: TBA
cf-feat-divine-castigation = Divine Castigation
cf-feat-divine-castigation-desc = Requires holy or unholy trait. Add your holy or unholy trait to heal or harm: TBA
cf-feat-divine-disharmony = Divine Disharmony
cf-feat-divine-disharmony-desc = Costs 1 action. Distract the faithful: TBA
cf-feat-divine-evolution = Divine Evolution
cf-feat-divine-evolution-desc = Requires a bloodline with divine spells. An extra slot for heal or harm: TBA
cf-feat-divine-grace = Divine Grace
cf-feat-divine-grace-desc = Reaction, automatic. +2 circumstance bonus to a save against a spell, when that would change the result.
cf-feat-divine-health = Divine Health
cf-feat-divine-health-desc = +2 status bonus to saves against disease and poison, and a success against either becomes a critical success. Allies in your aura have +1 status bonus to those saves.
cf-feat-divine-infusion = Divine Infusion
cf-feat-divine-infusion-desc = Costs 1 action. If your next spell is Heal or Harm restoring Hit Points to one creature, its melee Strikes deal 1d6 more vitality or void damage for 6 seconds, 2d6 from rank 5.
cf-feat-diving-armor = Diving Armor
cf-feat-diving-armor-desc = Requires armor innovation. This option: TBA
cf-feat-domain-acumen = Domain Acumen
cf-feat-domain-acumen-desc = A domain spell from your mystery. Domains are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-domain-initiate = Domain Initiate
cf-feat-domain-initiate-desc = Pick one of your deity's domains, and gain its domain spell and a Focus Point.
cf-feat-double-shot = Double Shot
cf-feat-double-shot-desc = Costs 2 actions. Shoot your target and the nearest other enemy you can see within 60 feet, each at -2 and at the same penalty. It needs two arrows.
cf-feat-double-slice = Double Slice
cf-feat-double-slice-desc = Right-click one creature with a melee weapon in each hand: one Strike with each, at your current multiple attack penalty. The second takes -2 unless it is agile. Costs 2 actions.
cf-feat-draconic-arrogance = Draconic Arrogance
cf-feat-draconic-arrogance-desc = Requires dragon instinct. +2 status bonus to saves against emotion effects while raging.
cf-feat-dragon-stance = Dragon Stance
cf-feat-dragon-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. Your fists become 1d10 bludgeoning dragon tail attacks (nonlethal), and you cross the first 5 feet of difficult terrain at full Speed. Backswing: TBA
cf-feat-draining-strike = Draining Strike
cf-feat-draining-strike-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-dread-striker = Dread Striker
cf-feat-dread-striker-desc = Frightened creatures are off-guard to your attacks.
cf-feat-dual-energy-heart = Dual Energy Heart
cf-feat-dual-energy-heart-desc = Requires Energy Heart. A second energy type: TBA
cf-feat-dual-form-weapon = Dual-Form Weapon
cf-feat-dual-form-weapon-desc = Requires weapon innovation. This option: TBA
cf-feat-dual-handed-assault = Dual-Handed Assault
cf-feat-dual-handed-assault-desc = Costs 1 action, a flourish. Strike with a one-handed weapon gripped for a moment in both hands, for a bigger damage die. Needs a free hand.
cf-feat-dual-studies = Dual Studies
cf-feat-dual-studies-desc = You and your eidolon each learn a skill. This one: TBA
cf-feat-dual-weapon-reload = Dual-Weapon Reload
cf-feat-dual-weapon-reload-desc = Reload with a weapon in each hand: TBA
cf-feat-dueling-parry = Dueling Parry
cf-feat-dueling-parry-desc = Costs 1 action. With a one-handed melee weapon and your other hand free, +2 circumstance bonus to AC for 6 seconds.
cf-feat-duo-dragon-kick = Duo Dragon Kick
cf-feat-duo-dragon-kick-desc = Requires construct innovation. Costs 2 actions. This option: TBA
cf-feat-efficient-alchemy-alchemist = Efficient Alchemy (Alchemist)
cf-feat-efficient-alchemy-alchemist-desc = Larger batches while crafting: TBA
cf-feat-elegant-buckler = Elegant Buckler
cf-feat-elegant-buckler-desc = A raised buckler gives +2 to AC, not +1. Panache when a creature critically misses you: TBA
cf-feat-elemental-defense = Elemental Defense
cf-feat-elemental-defense-desc = Costs 1 action. Resistance when you cast an elemental spell: TBA
cf-feat-elemental-fist = Elemental Fist
cf-feat-elemental-fist-desc = Requires Inner Upheaval. Inner Upheaval's extra damage as an element. It is always force here: TBA
cf-feat-elemental-summons = Elemental Summons
cf-feat-elemental-summons-desc = Swap a prepared spell for Summon Elemental. That spell is not in the game: TBA
cf-feat-eliminate-red-herrings = Eliminate Red Herrings
cf-feat-eliminate-red-herrings-desc = Fewer critical failures on an investigation. Investigations do not exist: TBA
cf-feat-emblazon-armament = Emblazon Armament
cf-feat-emblazon-armament-desc = Costs 3 actions, then 10 minutes before the next. Draw your deity's symbol on the weapon or shield in your active hand. A follower of your deity deals 1 more damage with the weapon, or the shield has 1 more Hardness for them. Both are status bonuses. Your last symbol fades.
cf-feat-embodimentofthe-balance = Embodiment of the Balance
cf-feat-embodimentofthe-balance-desc = Add heal and harm to your apparition spells.
cf-feat-emergency-targe = Emergency Targe
cf-feat-emergency-targe-desc = Requires sparkling targe hybrid study. Reaction, automatic. When a melee Strike would hit you, you raise a shield you are holding, and its bonus counts against that Strike. Against spell attacks and failed saves, and casting the shield spell: TBA
cf-feat-emotional-push = Emotional Push
cf-feat-emotional-push-desc = Automatic. An enemy that fails its save against your emotion spell is off-guard to you for 6 seconds. It does not use your reaction, where the rules ask for it.
cf-feat-enduring-alchemy = Enduring Alchemy
cf-feat-enduring-alchemy-desc = An elixir you make with Quick Alchemy stays potent for 12 seconds, where it lasts 6. A bomb does not.
cf-feat-energized-spark = Energized Spark
cf-feat-energized-spark-desc = Change what your spark deals. This one: TBA
cf-feat-energy-ablation = Energy Ablation
cf-feat-energy-ablation-desc = Costs 1 action. A spellshape. If your next spell deals acid, cold, electricity, fire, force, sonic, vitality or void damage, you gain resistance to that energy equal to the spell's rank for 6 seconds. The rules let you choose which energy.
cf-feat-energy-heart = Energy Heart
cf-feat-energy-heart-desc = Your eidolon deals energy damage. This one: TBA
cf-feat-energy-interceptor = Energy Interceptor
cf-feat-energy-interceptor-desc = Requires Intercept Attack. You can also take acid, cold, electricity, fire or sonic damage for an ally.
cf-feat-engraving-strike = Engraving Strike
cf-feat-engraving-strike-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-animist = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-animist-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-druid = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-druid-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-magus = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-magus-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-sorcerer = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-sorcerer-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-thaumaturge = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-thaumaturge-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-witch = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-witch-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-wizard = Enhanced Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-familiar-wizard-desc = Requires a familiar. TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-glyph-familiar = Enhanced Glyph Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-glyph-familiar-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enhanced-undead-familiar = Enhanced Undead Familiar
cf-feat-enhanced-undead-familiar-desc = Requires a familiar. More familiar abilities, which are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-enjoythe-show = Enjoy the Show
cf-feat-enjoythe-show-desc = Performing in combat is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-esoteric-polymath = Esoteric Polymath
cf-feat-esoteric-polymath-desc = Requires polymath muse. Each day you pick one more signature spell, on the Daily tab. A book of spells to learn new ones from: TBA
cf-feat-esoteric-warden = Esoteric Warden
cf-feat-esoteric-warden-desc = Requires Exploit Vulnerability. A bonus against the creature you exploit: TBA
cf-feat-eventhe-odds = Even the Odds
cf-feat-eventhe-odds-desc = Free action. Panache while flanked. Real time has no turns to set it off: TBA
cf-feat-exacting-strike = Exacting Strike
cf-feat-exacting-strike-desc = Automatic. When you already have a multiple attack penalty, a Strike that misses does not raise it. A critical miss still does.
cf-feat-expanded-domain-initiate = Expanded Domain Initiate
cf-feat-expanded-domain-initiate-desc = Requires Domain Initiate. Pick another of your deity's domains, and gain its domain spell and a Focus Point.
cf-feat-expanded-senses = Expanded Senses
cf-feat-expanded-senses-desc = Your eidolon gains senses. This one: TBA
cf-feat-expansive-spellstrike = Expansive Spellstrike
cf-feat-expansive-spellstrike-desc = Requires Spellstrike. Area spells through a Spellstrike: TBA
cf-feat-exploding-bullet = Exploding Bullet
cf-feat-exploding-bullet-desc = Requires volatile spark hybrid study. Costs 1 action. TBA
cf-feat-exploit-blunder = Exploit Blunder
cf-feat-exploit-blunder-desc = Reaction. Step when a foe you studied misses you. Reactions cannot move you yet: TBA
cf-feat-explosive-leap = Explosive Leap
cf-feat-explosive-leap-desc = Costs 1 action. Unstable. A blast from your innovation throws you 30 feet the way you are facing. A construct innovation cannot do it for you: TBA
cf-feat-extend-boost = Extend Boost
cf-feat-extend-boost-desc = A link spell. This one: TBA
cf-feat-extravagant-parry = Extravagant Parry
cf-feat-extravagant-parry-desc = Costs 1 action. +1 circumstance bonus to AC for 6 seconds. The +2 with a free hand, and panache when an attack misses: TBA
cf-feat-faithful-steed = Faithful Steed
cf-feat-faithful-steed-desc = An animal companion as a mount. Mounts are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-fake-out = Fake Out
cf-feat-fake-out-desc = Reaction. Help an ally attack by pretending to fire: TBA
cf-feat-familiar-magus = Familiar
cf-feat-familiar-magus-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-familiar-sorcerer = Familiar
cf-feat-familiar-sorcerer-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-familiar-thaumaturge = Familiar
cf-feat-familiar-thaumaturge-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-familiar-wizard = Familiar
cf-feat-familiar-wizard-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-familiars-language = Familiar's Language
cf-feat-familiars-language-desc = Requires a familiar. Your familiar's abilities are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-far-lobber = Far Lobber
cf-feat-far-lobber-desc = A bomb you throw has a range increment of 30 feet, where it has 20.
cf-feat-far-shot = Far Shot
cf-feat-far-shot-desc = Your weapons' range increments are doubled.
cf-feat-favored-prey = Favored Prey
cf-feat-favored-prey-desc = Bonuses against a kind of creature. Real time has no initiative to set it off: TBA
cf-feat-favored-terrain = Favored Terrain
cf-feat-favored-terrain-desc = Pick a terrain. Its non-magical difficult terrain does not slow you: plants for forest and plains, snow for arctic, stone and snow for mountain, stone and tight spaces for underground, water and plants for swamp, water for aquatic, sand for desert. The game has no map of terrains, so it counts anywhere. The second benefit from unimpeded journey: TBA
cf-feat-fermenting-liquors = Fermenting Liquors
cf-feat-fermenting-liquors-desc = Costs 1 action. Heal an ally with a daily drink: TBA
cf-feat-finishing-follow-through = Finishing Follow-Through
cf-feat-finishing-follow-through-desc = A finisher that drops its target gives your panache back.
cf-feat-flamboyant-athlete = Flamboyant Athlete
cf-feat-flamboyant-athlete-desc = Requires expert in Athletics. Climb, swim and jump with panache: TBA
cf-feat-flashy-dodge = Flashy Dodge
cf-feat-flashy-dodge-desc = Reaction, automatic. When an attack from a creature you can see would land and +2 circumstance to AC would change that, you dodge, and gain panache if it misses. Not while encumbered.
cf-feat-flexible-studies = Flexible Studies
cf-feat-flexible-studies-desc = You are trained in one skill of your choice for the day. Change it on the character sheet's Daily tab: the new skill takes over at your next long rest.
cf-feat-flood-stance = Flood Stance
cf-feat-flood-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. Holding your breath in a fight. Water is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-flurryof-maneuvers = Flurry of Maneuvers
cf-feat-flurryof-maneuvers-desc = Requires expert in Athletics. Maneuvers as part of Flurry of Blows: TBA
cf-feat-flying-blade = Flying Blade
cf-feat-flying-blade-desc = Requires Precise Strike. Precise Strike also counts for thrown weapon Strikes with an agile or finesse weapon, finishers included. The rules limit it to the first range increment.
cf-feat-flying-kick = Flying Kick
cf-feat-flying-kick-desc = Costs 2 actions. You leap up to 15 feet at an enemy and Strike it with an unarmed attack.
cf-feat-flying-tackle = Flying Tackle
cf-feat-flying-tackle-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. Costs 2 actions. Run, jump, and trip: TBA
cf-feat-focused-fascination = Focused Fascination
cf-feat-focused-fascination-desc = Requires Fascinating Performance. Performing in combat is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-followthe-threadsof-fate = Follow the Threads of Fate
cf-feat-followthe-threadsof-fate-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-force-fang = Force Fang
cf-feat-force-fang-desc = Your attack becomes pure force for 1d4+1 force damage, and it recharges Spellstrike. Costs a Focus Point.
cf-feat-forest-passage = Forest Passage
cf-feat-forest-passage-desc = Requires leaf order. Bushes, vines, undergrowth and other plants and fungi are not difficult terrain for you.
cf-feat-foretell-harm = Foretell Harm
cf-feat-foretell-harm-desc = Free action. Cursebound. Within 6 seconds of casting a damaging spell that is not a cantrip, a creature within 60 feet takes twice that spell's rank in damage of the same type. It lands at once, where the rules wait for the target's next turn.
cf-feat-form-control = Form Control
cf-feat-form-control-desc = Requires Untamed Form. Costs 1 action. A spellshape. Your next Untamed Form is 2 ranks lower, at least rank 1, and lasts an hour. Up to level 5 that is always the pest.
cf-feat-fortifying-knock = Fortifying Knock
cf-feat-fortifying-knock-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-furious-finish = Furious Finish
cf-feat-furious-finish-desc = Costs 1 action, while raging. A Strike that deals 1 more damage for each round your Rage had left, up to 10. Your Rage then ends and you are fatigued for 1 minute.
cf-feat-gadget-specialist = Gadget Specialist
cf-feat-gadget-specialist-desc = Requires expert in Crafting. Daily gadgets: TBA
cf-feat-galloping-launch-ranger = Galloping Launch
cf-feat-galloping-launch-ranger-desc = Costs 1 action. A thrown weapon from a mount. Mounts are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-ghostly-resonance = Ghostly Resonance
cf-feat-ghostly-resonance-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-ghostly-stride = Ghostly Stride
cf-feat-ghostly-stride-desc = Costs 1 action. For 3 seconds you can leave an enemy's reach at no cost and without setting off a reaction. Creatures do not block each other here, so you could already pass through them.
cf-feat-glean-lore = Glean Lore
cf-feat-glean-lore-desc = Costs 1 action. Ask the divine for information. That needs a game master: TBA
cf-feat-glider-form = Glider Form
cf-feat-glider-form-desc = Costs 1 action. Your eidolon glides. This one: TBA
cf-feat-glyph-familiar = Glyph Familiar
cf-feat-glyph-familiar-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-goading-feint = Goading Feint
cf-feat-goading-feint-desc = Requires trained in Deception. A Feint that throws off the target's next attack: TBA
cf-feat-grasping-spirits-spell = Grasping Spirits Spell
cf-feat-grasping-spirits-spell-desc = Costs 1 action, once per 10 minutes. A spellshape. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Pulling the target toward you: TBA
cf-feat-guarded-movement = Guarded Movement
cf-feat-guarded-movement-desc = +4 circumstance to AC against reactions set off by your movement.
cf-feat-guardians-deflection-swashbuckler = Guardian's Deflection (Swashbuckler)
cf-feat-guardians-deflection-swashbuckler-desc = Reaction, automatic. With a hand free, give an ally next to you +2 circumstance to AC against an attack you can see, when that turns the hit into a miss.
cf-feat-guiding-shot = Guiding Shot
cf-feat-guiding-shot-desc = Costs 1 action. A ranged Strike that helps the next attacker: TBA
cf-feat-haft-striker-stance-fighter = Haft Striker Stance
cf-feat-haft-striker-stance-fighter-desc = Costs 1 action. Strike with the haft of a two-handed weapon: TBA
cf-feat-haft-striker-stance-ranger = Haft Striker Stance
cf-feat-haft-striker-stance-ranger-desc = Costs 1 action. Strike with the haft of a two-handed weapon: TBA
cf-feat-haft-striker-stance-rogue = Haft Striker Stance
cf-feat-haft-striker-stance-rogue-desc = Costs 1 action. Strike with the haft of a two-handed weapon: TBA
cf-feat-hampering-stance = Hampering Stance
cf-feat-hampering-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. While you stay in this stance, the ground within 5 feet of you is difficult terrain for your enemies.
cf-feat-haphazard-repair = Haphazard Repair
cf-feat-haphazard-repair-desc = Costs 1 action. Quickly fix your innovation. This option: TBA
cf-feat-harming-hands = Harming Hands
cf-feat-harming-hands-desc = When you cast harm, you roll d10s instead of d8s.
cf-feat-harmonize-self = Harmonize Self
cf-feat-harmonize-self-desc = Requires Qi Spells. You gain the harmonize self qi spell: regain 8 Hit Points, 16 at level 5. Curing a poison or disease with it: TBA
cf-feat-haunt-ingenuity = Haunt Ingenuity
cf-feat-haunt-ingenuity-desc = Notice haunts without Searching. Haunts are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-head-stomp = Head Stomp
cf-feat-head-stomp-desc = Costs 1 action. An unarmed Strike against a prone creature. On a hit it is stupefied 1, or 2 on a critical hit, and off-guard.
cf-feat-healing-bomb = Healing Bomb
cf-feat-healing-bomb-desc = Throw an elixir of life at an ally: TBA
cf-feat-healing-hands = Healing Hands
cf-feat-healing-hands-desc = When you cast heal, you roll d10s instead of d8s.
cf-feat-heaven-earth-encompassing-sleeves = Heaven-Earth Encompassing Sleeves
cf-feat-heaven-earth-encompassing-sleeves-desc = Requires unfurling brocade hybrid study. Clothing that stores things: TBA
cf-feat-hitthe-dirt = Hit the Dirt!
cf-feat-hitthe-dirt-desc = Reaction, automatic. When a ranged Strike from a creature you can see would hit you, you throw yourself down: +2 circumstance to AC against it, when that turns it into a miss, and you end up prone. The Leap itself: TBA
cf-feat-homing-beacon = Homing Beacon
cf-feat-homing-beacon-desc = Amps from feats are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-hunted-shot = Hunted Shot
cf-feat-hunted-shot-desc = Costs 1 action. Two shots at your hunted prey, the second nocked from your quiver. Their damage is not combined against resistance.
cf-feat-hunters-aim = Hunter's Aim
cf-feat-hunters-aim-desc = Costs 2 actions. A ranged Strike at your prey with +2 to the attack roll, ignoring its concealment. Ignoring lesser cover: TBA
cf-feat-hurlatthe-horizon = Hurl at the Horizon
cf-feat-hurlatthe-horizon-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-hymnof-healing = Hymn of Healing
cf-feat-hymnof-healing-desc = A focus spell: you or an ally regains 2 Hit Points and gains 2 temporary Hit Points every 6 seconds for 24 seconds.
cf-feat-impaling-finisher = Impaling Finisher
cf-feat-impaling-finisher-desc = Costs 1 action. A finisher. Strike your target and an enemy standing straight behind it, at the same penalty. It counts as two attacks. Any weapon will do, where the rules ask for piercing or bludgeoning. Use your weapon in hand (Z) to switch to it, and Alt+Z to perform it.
cf-feat-improvise-admixture = Improvise Admixture
cf-feat-improvise-admixture-desc = Costs 1 action, once a day. A Crafting check against the DC for your level gives back versatile vials, up to your most: 3 on a critical success, 2 on a success, 1 on a failure.
cf-feat-in-tune = In Tune
cf-feat-in-tune-desc = Requires maestro muse. Costs 1 action. Allies share your Performance. Compositions are not spells yet: TBA
cf-feat-incriminating-spell = Incriminating Spell
cf-feat-incriminating-spell-desc = Costs 1 action. Blame someone else for a mental spell: TBA
cf-feat-initiate-warden = Initiate Warden
cf-feat-initiate-warden-desc = A warden spell. Those do not exist yet: TBA
cf-feat-instant-backup = Instant Backup
cf-feat-instant-backup-desc = Reaction. Draw a weapon when a gun misfires. TBA
cf-feat-intimidating-strike-barbarian = Intimidating Strike
cf-feat-intimidating-strike-barbarian-desc = Costs 2 actions. A melee Strike that frightens the target if it deals damage: frightened 1, or 2 on a critical hit.
cf-feat-intimidating-strike-fighter = Intimidating Strike
cf-feat-intimidating-strike-fighter-desc = Costs 2 actions. A melee Strike that frightens the target if it deals damage: frightened 1, or 2 on a critical hit.
cf-feat-invert-harm = Invert Harm
cf-feat-invert-harm-desc = Harm can heal the living. Mastery of Life and Death is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-invigorating-elixir = Invigorating Elixir
cf-feat-invigorating-elixir-desc = An elixir that also treats a condition: TBA
cf-feat-invisible-ink = Invisible Ink
cf-feat-invisible-ink-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-iron-repercussions = Iron Repercussions
cf-feat-iron-repercussions-desc = Requires obedience cause. Iron Command's mental damage is persistent: 1d6, or 2d6 from level 5. It is always persistent, where the rules let you choose each time.
cf-feat-knowledgeof-shapes = Knowledge of Shapes
cf-feat-knowledgeof-shapes-desc = Requires Reach Spell or Widen Spell. Use one as a free action: TBA
cf-feat-known-weaknesses = Known Weaknesses
cf-feat-known-weaknesses-desc = When you Devise a Stratagem, you also Recall Knowledge about the target at no extra cost. The +1 to attacks on a critical success: TBA
cf-feat-larger-than-life-guardian = Larger Than Life (Guardian)
cf-feat-larger-than-life-guardian-desc = Count as larger in heavy armor. Size does not change maneuvers yet: TBA
cf-feat-leading-dance = Leading Dance
cf-feat-leading-dance-desc = Requires trained in Performance. Costs 1 action. Sweep a foe along with you: TBA
cf-feat-leapthe-falls = Leap the Falls
cf-feat-leapthe-falls-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-leshy-familiar = Leshy Familiar
cf-feat-leshy-familiar-desc = Requires leaf order. A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-leshy-familiar-secrets = Leshy Familiar Secrets
cf-feat-leshy-familiar-secrets-desc = Requires leaf order. One more familiar ability, from a leshy list. Familiar abilities are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-lie-detector = Lie Detector
cf-feat-lie-detector-desc = Requires empiricism or interrogation methodology. Better at catching lies: TBA
cf-feat-lifelink-surge = Lifelink Surge
cf-feat-lifelink-surge-desc = A link spell. This one: TBA
cf-feat-lightning-swap-exemplar = Lightning Swap
cf-feat-lightning-swap-exemplar-desc = Costs 1 action. Stow and draw several items: TBA
cf-feat-lightning-swap-fighter = Lightning Swap
cf-feat-lightning-swap-fighter-desc = Costs 1 action. Stow and draw several items: TBA
cf-feat-lingering-composition = Lingering Composition
cf-feat-lingering-composition-desc = Requires maestro muse. A composition already lasts a minute here, so this adds nothing. A Performance check for a longer one: TBA
cf-feat-linked-focus = Linked Focus
cf-feat-linked-focus-desc = Requires arcane bond and curriculum spells. TBA
cf-feat-long-distance-taunt = Long-Distance Taunt
cf-feat-long-distance-taunt-desc = Taunt an enemy within 120 feet.
cf-feat-longshanks-slam = Longshanks Slam
cf-feat-longshanks-slam-desc = Costs 1 action. Quick Alchemy and a Strike on a larger foe. Quick Alchemy is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-loremasters-etude = Loremaster's Etude
cf-feat-loremasters-etude-desc = Requires enigma muse. A focus spell, cast for free: when your Arcana, Lore, Nature, Occultism, Religion or Society check falls short, you roll again and keep the better. The rules limit it to Recall Knowledge, and let it help an ally: TBA
cf-feat-lunge = Lunge
cf-feat-lunge-desc = Costs 1 action. A melee Strike with 5 feet more reach. Using it for a disarm, shove or trip: TBA
cf-feat-magical-understudy = Magical Understudy
cf-feat-magical-understudy-desc = Your eidolon casts cantrips. This one: TBA
cf-feat-maguss-analysis = Magus's Analysis
cf-feat-maguss-analysis-desc = Requires Spellstrike. Costs 1 action. Recall Knowledge about a creature, and recharge Spellstrike.
cf-feat-martial-performance = Martial Performance
cf-feat-martial-performance-desc = Requires warrior muse. A composition already lasts a minute here, so this adds nothing. Damage with a Strike extending it: TBA
cf-feat-mature-animal-companion-druid = Mature Animal Companion (Druid)
cf-feat-mature-animal-companion-druid-desc = Requires Animal Companion. Your companion already acts without being commanded. Its mature size and statistics: TBA
cf-feat-meddling-futures = Meddling Futures
cf-feat-meddling-futures-desc = Free action. Spirits guide your next action: TBA
cf-feat-megaton-strike = Megaton Strike
cf-feat-megaton-strike-desc = Costs 2 actions. A melee Strike with one extra damage die. An unstable action, so your innovation may stop working.
cf-feat-meldinto-eidolon = Meld into Eidolon
cf-feat-meldinto-eidolon-desc = Costs 3 actions. Become your eidolon. This one: TBA
cf-feat-melodious-spell = Melodious Spell
cf-feat-melodious-spell-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell does not set off reactions.
cf-feat-mental-balm = Mental Balm
cf-feat-mental-balm-desc = Amps from feats are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-mental-buffer = Mental Buffer
cf-feat-mental-buffer-desc = Mental resistance equal to half your level, at least 1. The increase while unleashed: TBA
cf-feat-mercy = Mercy
cf-feat-mercy-desc = Requires Lay on Hands. Choose body, grace or mind. You can cast Lay on Hands with 2 actions to also end one condition on the target. Body: blinded, dazzled, deafened or enfeebled. Grace: clumsy. Mind: frightened or stupefied. It always works, where the rules make it a counteract check. Sickened, grabbed, paralyzed and fleeing: TBA
cf-feat-mobile-thralls = Mobile Thralls
cf-feat-mobile-thralls-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-mobility = Mobility
cf-feat-mobility-desc = Walking out of an enemy's reach needs no action and does not provoke.
cf-feat-momentof-clarity = Moment of Clarity
cf-feat-momentof-clarity-desc = Costs 1 action. Use a concentrate action while raging, this turn. Real time has no turns to end it: TBA
cf-feat-monastic-archer-stance = Monastic Archer Stance
cf-feat-monastic-archer-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. Monk abilities with a bow: TBA
cf-feat-monastic-weaponry = Monastic Weaponry
cf-feat-monastic-weaponry-desc = Train with monk weapons. Weapons do not have the monk trait yet: TBA
cf-feat-monster-hunter = Monster Hunter
cf-feat-monster-hunter-desc = When you Hunt Prey, you also Recall Knowledge about it at no extra cost. The +1 to your and your allies' next attack on a critical success: TBA
cf-feat-monster-warden = Monster Warden
cf-feat-monster-warden-desc = Requires Monster Hunter. Requires Monster Hunter. A defense against your prey: TBA
cf-feat-mountain-stance = Mountain Stance
cf-feat-mountain-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. +4 item bonus to AC, no Dexterity to AC, and 5 feet less Speed. Your only Strikes are 1d8 bludgeoning falling stone attacks (forceful, nonlethal). +2 circumstance to your DC against Shove, Trip, Grapple, Disarm and Reposition. The requirement to touch the ground: TBA
cf-feat-mug = Mug
cf-feat-mug-desc = Costs 2 actions. A Strike that also Steals: TBA
cf-feat-multifarious-muse = Multifarious Muse
cf-feat-multifarious-muse-desc = A feat from another muse: TBA
cf-feat-munitions-crafter = Munitions Crafter
cf-feat-munitions-crafter-desc = Make daily bullets and bombs: TBA
cf-feat-muscle-barrier = Muscle Barrier
cf-feat-muscle-barrier-desc = A grave spell. This one: TBA
cf-feat-natural-conduit = Natural Conduit
cf-feat-natural-conduit-desc = Requires warden spells. Costs 1 action. Cast through an animal: TBA
cf-feat-nimble-dodge = Nimble Dodge
cf-feat-nimble-dodge-desc = Reaction, automatic. When an attack from a creature you can see would land and +2 circumstance to AC would change that, you dodge. Not while encumbered.
cf-feat-nimble-reprisal = Nimble Reprisal
cf-feat-nimble-reprisal-desc = Requires justice cause. Retributive Strike with a ranged weapon or a Step: TBA
cf-feat-no-escape = No Escape
cf-feat-no-escape-desc = Reaction, automatic, while raging. When an enemy leaves your reach, you rush after it, up to your Speed, and end beside it. Your move sets off no reactions.
cf-feat-no-no-i-created-you = No! No! I Created You!
cf-feat-no-no-i-created-you-desc = Requires a construct companion. Reaction. This option: TBA
cf-feat-nonlethal-spell = Nonlethal Spell
cf-feat-nonlethal-spell-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next damaging spell is nonlethal: TBA
cf-feat-not-so-fast = Not So Fast!
cf-feat-not-so-fast-desc = Requires Hampering Stance. Reaction. Stop a foe that tries to pass: TBA
cf-feat-nudgethe-scales = Nudge the Scales
cf-feat-nudgethe-scales-desc = Costs 1 action. Cursebound. Heal a creature within 30 feet for 2 Hit Points plus double your level. Choosing life or death each day: TBA
cf-feat-numbing-spice-exhalation = Numbing Spice Exhalation
cf-feat-numbing-spice-exhalation-desc = Spiced food that lets you breathe fire: TBA
cf-feat-oathofthe-avenger = Oath of the Avenger
cf-feat-oathofthe-avenger-desc = Requires Lay on Hands. Punish those who harm the innocent: TBA
cf-feat-oathofthe-defender = Oath of the Defender
cf-feat-oathofthe-defender-desc = Allies in your aura resist a chosen kind of creature. Daily choices are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-oathofthe-slayer = Oath of the Slayer
cf-feat-oathofthe-slayer-desc = Extra spirit damage against a chosen kind of creature. Daily choices are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-observational-analysis = Observational Analysis
cf-feat-observational-analysis-desc = Requires Combat Assessment. Better Recall Knowledge in a fight: TBA
cf-feat-occult-evolution = Occult Evolution
cf-feat-occult-evolution-desc = Requires a bloodline with occult spells. A temporary mental spell: TBA
cf-feat-officers-medical-training = Officer's Medical Training
cf-feat-officers-medical-training-desc = Trained in Medicine. Using Intelligence for it: TBA
cf-feat-oil-fire = Oil Fire
cf-feat-oil-fire-desc = Requires armor innovation. Costs 1 action. This option: TBA
cf-feat-onefor-all = One for All
cf-feat-onefor-all-desc = Requires trained in Diplomacy. Costs 1 action. Aid an ally with Diplomacy: TBA
cf-feat-ongoing-investigation = Ongoing Investigation
cf-feat-ongoing-investigation-desc = Investigate while exploring. Exploration activities are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-ongoing-selfishness = Ongoing Selfishness
cf-feat-ongoing-selfishness-desc = Requires desecration cause. Selfish Shield keeps working against that enemy: TBA
cf-feat-onlythe-worthy = Only the Worthy
cf-feat-onlythe-worthy-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-oracular-warning = Oracular Warning
cf-feat-oracular-warning-desc = Free action. Cursebound. You and allies within 20 feet gain temporary Hit Points equal to half your level for a minute. Used by hand, where the rules set it off as a fight begins.
cf-feat-order-explorer = Order Explorer
cf-feat-order-explorer-desc = Choose a level 1 feat of an order other than your own: Animal Companion, Leshy Familiar, Storm Born or Untamed Form. You count as a member of that order for later feats. You can take this once.
cf-feat-order-magic = Order Magic
cf-feat-order-magic-desc = Requires Order Explorer. You gain the order spell of the order you joined: heal animal, cornucopia, tempest surge or untamed form.
cf-feat-osteo-armaments = Osteo Armaments
cf-feat-osteo-armaments-desc = Costs 1 action. Make a weapon of bone: TBA
cf-feat-overextending-feint = Overextending Feint
cf-feat-overextending-feint-desc = Requires trained in Deception. Costs 1 action. A Feint that does not leave the target off-guard: on a success it takes -2 circumstance to its next attack roll against you within 6 seconds, and to all of them for 6 seconds on a critical success. The rules let you choose this on any Feint: here it is its own action.
cf-feat-oversized-throw = Oversized Throw
cf-feat-oversized-throw-desc = Costs 2 actions. Hurl a boulder or a table at a foe: TBA
cf-feat-overwhelming-harm = Overwhelming Harm
cf-feat-overwhelming-harm-desc = A longer area on harm. Three-action harm is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-paired-link = Paired Link
cf-feat-paired-link-desc = Share effects with an ally through a charm: TBA
cf-feat-paired-shots = Paired Shots
cf-feat-paired-shots-desc = Costs 2 actions. Fire two one-handed firearms or crossbows at once. The game has no one-handed ranged weapon: TBA
cf-feat-panicthe-dead = Panic the Dead
cf-feat-panicthe-dead-desc = An undead that fails its save against your Heal is also frightened 1. Fleeing on a critical failure: TBA
cf-feat-parting-shot = Parting Shot
cf-feat-parting-shot-desc = Costs 2 actions. You hop 5 feet back from your target and shoot it. It is off-guard against the shot.
cf-feat-pattern-flight = Pattern Flight
cf-feat-pattern-flight-desc = Costs 2 actions. This one: TBA
cf-feat-pernicious-poison = Pernicious Poison
cf-feat-pernicious-poison-desc = A poison that splashes on a save. Poisons are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-personalized-poisoning = Personalized Poisoning
cf-feat-personalized-poisoning-desc = Requires alchemical sciences methodology. Study a target's weakness to poison: TBA
cf-feat-personof-interest = Person of Interest
cf-feat-personof-interest-desc = Costs 1 action, once every 10 minutes. Pick a creature within 60 feet: for a minute, Devise a Stratagem against it costs no action.
cf-feat-phalanx-formation = Phalanx Formation
cf-feat-phalanx-formation-desc = Fight in formation: TBA
cf-feat-pistol-twirl = Pistol Twirl
cf-feat-pistol-twirl-desc = Requires trained in Deception. Costs 1 action. Feint at range: TBA
cf-feat-plant-banner = Plant Banner
cf-feat-plant-banner-desc = Costs 1 action. A use of your banner: TBA
cf-feat-plant-empathy = Plant Empathy
cf-feat-plant-empathy-desc = Speak to plants: TBA
cf-feat-plant-evidence = Plant Evidence
cf-feat-plant-evidence-desc = Requires Pickpocket. Costs 1 action. Slip an item onto someone: TBA
cf-feat-plummeting-roll = Plummeting Roll
cf-feat-plummeting-roll-desc = Requires trained in Acrobatics. Land on your feet after a fall and move: TBA
cf-feat-point-blank-stance = Point Blank Stance
cf-feat-point-blank-stance-desc = Ignore the volley penalty and gain +2 damage with ranged Strikes inside the first range increment.
cf-feat-poison-resistance-alchemist = Poison Resistance
cf-feat-poison-resistance-alchemist-desc = Poison resistance equal to half your level, and +1 status bonus to saves against poison.
cf-feat-poison-resistance-druid = Poison Resistance
cf-feat-poison-resistance-druid-desc = Poison resistance equal to half your level, and +1 status to saves against poison.
cf-feat-poison-weapon = Poison Weapon
cf-feat-poison-weapon-desc = Costs 1 action. Poison your weapon. Injury poisons are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-portentsofthe-haruspex = Portents of the Haruspex
cf-feat-portentsofthe-haruspex-desc = Reaction. Learn from a creature's fall: TBA
cf-feat-powerful-shove = Powerful Shove
cf-feat-powerful-shove-desc = Requires Aggressive Block or Brutish Shove. Shoving larger creatures, and damage when a shoved creature hits something. Size is not checked here, and a shove does not know what stopped it: TBA
cf-feat-predictable = Predictable!
cf-feat-predictable-desc = Costs 1 action. Read a foe's next move: TBA
cf-feat-premonitionof-avoidance = Premonition of Avoidance
cf-feat-premonitionof-avoidance-desc = Reaction, automatic. +2 circumstance to a save against a trap, when that would improve the result.
cf-feat-primal-evolution = Primal Evolution
cf-feat-primal-evolution-desc = Requires a bloodline with primal spells. An extra slot of your highest rank that only Summon Animal can use. A slot tied to one spell is not built: TBA
cf-feat-propelling-sorcery = Propelling Sorcery
cf-feat-propelling-sorcery-desc = When your blood magic helps you, you can also leave an enemy's reach in the next 3 seconds at no cost and without setting off a reaction. The rules make it a choice in place of the bloodline's effect, and let you move a target 5 feet instead.
cf-feat-prototype-companion = Prototype Companion
cf-feat-prototype-companion-desc = A clockwork construct companion. It follows you and fights for you, and goes first for the creature you point at.
cf-feat-proud-nail = Proud Nail
cf-feat-proud-nail-desc = Costs 1 action. A melee Strike with one extra damage die, against an enemy that ignored your Taunt.
cf-feat-psi-burst = Psi Burst
cf-feat-psi-burst-desc = Costs 1 action. A creature within 30 feet takes 1d4 bludgeoning, basic Reflex, with 1d4 more at level 3 and level 5.
cf-feat-psi-strikes = Psi Strikes
cf-feat-psi-strikes-desc = Free action, automatic. After you cast a spell, a cantrip included, your next Strike that hits within 6 seconds deals 1d6 force damage more. Lasting for as long as your psyche is unleashed: TBA
cf-feat-psychic-rapport = Psychic Rapport
cf-feat-psychic-rapport-desc = A bonus to social skills after a mental spell: TBA
cf-feat-punishing-shove = Punishing Shove
cf-feat-punishing-shove-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. A successful Shove also deals your Strength modifier in bludgeoning damage, or double on a critical success.
cf-feat-qi-spells = Qi Spells
cf-feat-qi-spells-desc = Choose a qi spell, a focus spell. Inner Upheaval: for 3 seconds your melee Strikes have +1 to attack and deal 1d6 more force damage. Qi Rush: for 3 seconds you move 30 feet faster, and you are concealed for 6. You can take this once.
cf-feat-quick-bomber = Quick Bomber
cf-feat-quick-bomber-desc = Costs 1 action. Make an acid versatile vial and throw it at a creature within 60 feet. Drawing a bomb you carry this way: TBA
cf-feat-quick-draw-gunslinger = Quick Draw
cf-feat-quick-draw-gunslinger-desc = Costs 1 action. You draw a weapon worn on your belt, back or neck into a free hand and Strike with it. A bow shoots the arrow it has nocked.
cf-feat-quick-draw-ranger = Quick Draw
cf-feat-quick-draw-ranger-desc = Costs 1 action. You draw a weapon worn on your belt, back or neck into a free hand and Strike with it. A bow shoots the arrow it has nocked.
cf-feat-quick-draw-rogue = Quick Draw
cf-feat-quick-draw-rogue-desc = Costs 1 action. You draw a weapon worn on your belt, back or neck into a free hand and Strike with it. A bow shoots the arrow it has nocked.
cf-feat-quick-reversal = Quick Reversal
cf-feat-quick-reversal-desc = Costs 1 action, after another attack this turn, with two enemies in your reach. Strike one and then the other at the same penalty. The second Strike does not add to your multiple attack penalty. They need not be flanking you.
cf-feat-raging-athlete = Raging Athlete
cf-feat-raging-athlete-desc = Requires expert in Athletics. Climb and swim while raging, which do not exist yet: TBA
cf-feat-raging-intimidation = Raging Intimidation
cf-feat-raging-intimidation-desc = Demoralize already works while raging. You gain the Intimidating Glare feat. Scare to Death is above level 5.
cf-feat-raging-thrower = Raging Thrower
cf-feat-raging-thrower-desc = Thrown weapon Strikes also get the extra damage from Rage.
cf-feat-raise-haft = Raise Haft
cf-feat-raise-haft-desc = You gain the Raise Haft action: with a melee weapon in both hands, +1 circumstance bonus to AC for 6 seconds, at 1 action. +2 with a weapon that already has the parry trait: TBA
cf-feat-raise-symbol = Raise Symbol
cf-feat-raise-symbol-desc = Costs 1 action. +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws for 6 seconds. There are no religious symbols to hold yet, so none is needed.
cf-feat-raisea-tome = Raise a Tome
cf-feat-raisea-tome-desc = Raise a book as a shield: TBA
cf-feat-rallying-anthem = Rallying Anthem
cf-feat-rallying-anthem-desc = A composition: for a minute, you and allies within 60 feet gain +1 status to AC and saves. Resistance to physical damage equal to half the rank: TBA
cf-feat-ranged-combatant = Ranged Combatant
cf-feat-ranged-combatant-desc = Your eidolon gains a ranged attack. This one: TBA
cf-feat-rapid-assessment = Rapid Assessment
cf-feat-rapid-assessment-desc = Free action. Real time has no initiative: TBA
cf-feat-rapid-response = Rapid Response
cf-feat-rapid-response-desc = Reaction, automatic. When an ally within 35 feet drops to 0 Hit Points, you rush to their side, up to your Speed. Your move sets off no reactions.
cf-feat-reach-spell-bard = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-bard-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reach-spell-cleric = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-cleric-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reach-spell-druid = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-druid-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reach-spell-oracle = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-oracle-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reach-spell-sorcerer = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-sorcerer-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reach-spell-witch = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-witch-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reach-spell-wizard = Reach Spell
cf-feat-reach-spell-wizard-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next spell with a range reaches 30 feet further. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-reachofthe-dead = Reach of the Dead
cf-feat-reachofthe-dead-desc = Free action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-reactive-dismissal = Reactive Dismissal
cf-feat-reactive-dismissal-desc = Reaction. Dismiss your eidolon to reduce damage. This one: TBA
cf-feat-reactive-pursuit = Reactive Pursuit
cf-feat-reactive-pursuit-desc = Reaction, automatic. When an enemy leaves your reach, you rush after it, up to your Speed, and end beside it. Your move sets off no reactions.
cf-feat-reactive-shield-fighter = Reactive Shield
cf-feat-reactive-shield-fighter-desc = Reaction. Raise a Shield when you are hit, if you are holding one.
cf-feat-reactive-shield-guardian = Reactive Shield
cf-feat-reactive-shield-guardian-desc = Reaction. Raise a Shield when you are hit, if you are holding one.
cf-feat-rebounding-toss = Rebounding Toss
cf-feat-rebounding-toss-desc = Costs 2 actions. A thrown weapon bounces to a second foe. A thrown weapon here is a real object in flight, which cannot be sent on: TBA
cf-feat-recharging-flurry = Recharging Flurry
cf-feat-recharging-flurry-desc = Requires twofold tine hybrid study. Costs 2 actions. Strike with both weapons, then recharge Spellstrike.
cf-feat-red-gold-mortality = Red-Gold Mortality
cf-feat-red-gold-mortality-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-reflective-ripple-stance = Reflective Ripple Stance
cf-feat-reflective-ripple-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. Your fists become 1d6 bludgeoning flowing wave attacks. +1 circumstance to your Athletics maneuvers and +2 to your DC against them. The rules limit both to Disarm and Trip.
cf-feat-regurgitate-mutagen = Regurgitate Mutagen
cf-feat-regurgitate-mutagen-desc = Costs 1 action. Spit a mutagen at a foe. Mutagens are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-reinforce-eidolon = Reinforce Eidolon
cf-feat-reinforce-eidolon-desc = You learn Reinforce Eidolon, a link cantrip.
cf-feat-relinquish-control = Relinquish Control
cf-feat-relinquish-control-desc = Free action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-remote-detonation = Remote Detonation
cf-feat-remote-detonation-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-restorative-strike = Restorative Strike
cf-feat-restorative-strike-desc = Costs 2 actions. Heal yourself and Strike: TBA
cf-feat-retreating-finisher = Retreating Finisher
cf-feat-retreating-finisher-desc = Costs 1 action. A finisher. If it misses, you can walk out of reach in the next 2 seconds at no cost and without setting off a reaction. Use your weapon in hand (Z) to switch to it, and Alt+Z to perform it.
cf-feat-reverse-engineer = Reverse Engineer
cf-feat-reverse-engineer-desc = Requires trained in Crafting. Learn formulas by taking items apart: TBA
cf-feat-revivifying-mutagen = Revivifying Mutagen
cf-feat-revivifying-mutagen-desc = Costs 1 action. End a mutagen to heal. Mutagens are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-ripand-tear-barbarian = Rip and Tear
cf-feat-ripand-tear-barbarian-desc = Requires animal instinct. Costs 1 action. While raging with your animal attack, if it deals piercing or slashing damage: an unarmed Strike at the creature you last attacked this turn. If it deals damage the target takes 1d6 persistent bleed.
cf-feat-ripand-tear-druid = Rip and Tear
cf-feat-ripand-tear-druid-desc = Requires untamed order. Costs 1 action. In a battle form whose attack deals piercing or slashing damage: an unarmed Strike at the creature you last attacked this turn. If it deals damage the target takes 1d6 persistent bleed.
cf-feat-risky-reload = Risky Reload
cf-feat-risky-reload-desc = Costs 1 action. Reload and Strike. TBA
cf-feat-ritesof-convocation = Rites of Convocation
cf-feat-ritesof-convocation-desc = You can cast Summon Animal in place of any spell you have prepared, at that spell's rank. The cast spends the prepared spell. It is the only summon spell in the game, so there is no choice of which: TBA
cf-feat-ritual-researcher = Ritual Researcher
cf-feat-ritual-researcher-desc = Requires enigma muse and expert in Occultism. Better at rituals. Rituals are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-rootto-life = Root to Life
cf-feat-rootto-life-desc = Stabilize a dying ally with a touch: TBA
cf-feat-rune-singer = Rune-Singer
cf-feat-rune-singer-desc = Requires trained in Performance. This one: TBA
cf-feat-rune-ward = Rune Ward
cf-feat-rune-ward-desc = Reaction. This one: TBA
cf-feat-runic-tattoo = Runic Tattoo
cf-feat-runic-tattoo-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-running-recharge = Running Recharge
cf-feat-running-recharge-desc = Costs 1 action. Move and recharge. Nothing stops you moving while you recharge, so this adds nothing yet: TBA
cf-feat-running-reload-gunslinger = Running Reload
cf-feat-running-reload-gunslinger-desc = Costs 1 action. Move and reload. Nothing stops you moving as you load, so this adds nothing yet: TBA
cf-feat-running-reload-ranger = Running Reload
cf-feat-running-reload-ranger-desc = Costs 1 action. Move and reload: TBA
cf-feat-rushing-goat-stance = Rushing Goat Stance
cf-feat-rushing-goat-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. Your only Strikes are 1d8 bludgeoning ramming horn attacks. The bonus damage after moving: TBA
cf-feat-sabotage = Sabotage
cf-feat-sabotage-desc = Costs 1 action. Damage a foe's equipment: TBA
cf-feat-sacral-lord-champion = Sacral Lord
cf-feat-sacral-lord-champion-desc = Requires trained in Occultism or Religion. Claim a territory as your own: TBA
cf-feat-sacral-lord-oracle = Sacral Lord
cf-feat-sacral-lord-oracle-desc = Requires trained in Occultism or Religion. Claim a territory as your own: TBA
cf-feat-sacred-ground = Sacred Ground
cf-feat-sacred-ground-desc = Requires harmful font or healing font. Consecrate an area for a while: TBA
cf-feat-sanctified-soul = Sanctified Soul
cf-feat-sanctified-soul-desc = Choose holy or unholy for your spirit damage: TBA
cf-feat-sap-life = Sap Life
cf-feat-sap-life-desc = When your Harm damages at least one living creature, you regain Hit Points equal to the spell's rank, if you are living.
cf-feat-scalpels-point = Scalpel's Point
cf-feat-scalpels-point-desc = Requires forensic medicine methodology. A critical hit with a stored Devise a Stratagem roll that deals piercing or slashing damage adds 1d6 persistent bleed.
cf-feat-scarsof-steel = Scars of Steel
cf-feat-scarsof-steel-desc = Requires fury instinct. Reaction, automatic, once per long rest. A critical hit with physical damage deals your Constitution modifier plus half your level less.
cf-feat-scatter-swarm = Scatter Swarm
cf-feat-scatter-swarm-desc = Costs 1 action. Scatter a swarm with your familiar. Familiar abilities are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-scoundrels-surprise = Scoundrel's Surprise
cf-feat-scoundrels-surprise-desc = Costs 1 action. Drop a disguise for a surprise. Disguises are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-scouts-warning-ranger = Scout's Warning
cf-feat-scouts-warning-ranger-desc = Free action. Warn allies. Real time has no initiative: TBA
cf-feat-scouts-warning-rogue = Scout's Warning
cf-feat-scouts-warning-rogue-desc = Free action. Warn allies. Real time has no initiative: TBA
cf-feat-scroll-thaumaturgy = Scroll Thaumaturgy
cf-feat-scroll-thaumaturgy-desc = Use any scroll. No scrolls exist yet: TBA
cf-feat-searing-restoration = Searing Restoration
cf-feat-searing-restoration-desc = Costs 1 action. Unstable. You or an adjacent creature regain 1d10 Hit Points, and 1d10 more at level 3 and every 2 levels after. They also get a flat check to stop persistent bleed. It heals constructs and undead too, and a construct innovation cannot use it for you: TBA
cf-feat-second-wind = Second Wind
cf-feat-second-wind-desc = A Rage gives its temporary Hit Points even if one did less than a minute ago. When it does, you are fatigued for 1 minute once that Rage ends, and cannot Rage while fatigued.
cf-feat-security = Security
cf-feat-security-desc = Requires Shields of the Spirit. A two-action version that puts a lasting spirit shield on one ally: TBA
cf-feat-seekthe-hidden-glyphs = Seek the Hidden Glyphs
cf-feat-seekthe-hidden-glyphs-desc = +1 to find magical traps: TBA
cf-feat-set-up-strike = Set-Up Strike
cf-feat-set-up-strike-desc = Costs 1 action. A Strike. On a hit, the target is off-guard for 6 seconds, longer than the next ally's attack the rules give.
cf-feat-shakeit-off = Shake it Off
cf-feat-shakeit-off-desc = Costs 1 action, while raging. Lower your frightened value by 1. Recovering from sickened: TBA
cf-feat-shared-stratagem = Shared Stratagem
cf-feat-shared-stratagem-desc = When a Strike with your stored Devise a Stratagem roll hits, the target is off-guard for 6 seconds to your nearest ally within 30 feet of it. The rules let you choose the ally, and end it with that ally's next attack.
cf-feat-shattering-spellstrike = Shattering Spellstrike
cf-feat-shattering-spellstrike-desc = Requires resurgent maelstrom hybrid study. Costs 2 actions. Break an improvised weapon for damage: TBA
cf-feat-shield-warfare = Shield Warfare
cf-feat-shield-warfare-desc = Your shield bash rolls a damage die one step larger.
cf-feat-shield-your-eyes = Shield Your Eyes
cf-feat-shield-your-eyes-desc = While your shield is raised, +2 circumstance bonus to saves against light and visual effects. Turning a critical failure into a failure: TBA
cf-feat-shielded-attrition = Shielded Attrition
cf-feat-shielded-attrition-desc = Costs 1 action. Raise a shield and draw reactions: TBA
cf-feat-shielded-recovery = Shielded Recovery
cf-feat-shielded-recovery-desc = Requires Officer's Medical Training. Treat wounds with your shield hand: TBA
cf-feat-shielded-stride = Shielded Stride
cf-feat-shielded-stride-desc = While your shield is raised, walking out of an enemy's reach needs no action and does not provoke.
cf-feat-shielding-taunt = Shielding Taunt
cf-feat-shielding-taunt-desc = Costs 1 action. Raise your shield and Taunt an enemy within 30 feet.
cf-feat-shooting-stars-stance = Shooting Stars Stance
cf-feat-shooting-stars-stance-desc = Requires Monastic Weaponry. Costs 1 action. Monk abilities with shuriken: TBA
cf-feat-shoulder-check = Shoulder Check
cf-feat-shoulder-check-desc = Costs 1 action. Strike with your armor: TBA
cf-feat-shrink-down = Shrink Down
cf-feat-shrink-down-desc = Costs 1 action. Your eidolon shrinks. This one: TBA
cf-feat-skilled-partner = Skilled Partner
cf-feat-skilled-partner-desc = Your eidolon gains skill feats. This one: TBA
cf-feat-slam-down = Slam Down
cf-feat-slam-down-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. Costs 2 actions. A melee Strike. If it deals damage, you roll Athletics against the target's Reflex DC to knock it prone. A critical success also deals 1d6 bludgeoning, and a critical failure knocks you prone.
cf-feat-sleek-reposition = Sleek Reposition
cf-feat-sleek-reposition-desc = Costs 1 action. A Strike with a finesse weapon or polearm that also Repositions. It needs a way to choose where the target goes: TBA
cf-feat-smithing-weapons = Smithing Weapons
cf-feat-smithing-weapons-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-smoke-bomb = Smoke Bomb
cf-feat-smoke-bomb-desc = A bomb that leaves smoke. Alchemical bombs are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-snagging-strike = Snagging Strike
cf-feat-snagging-strike-desc = Automatic. A Strike that hits while you have a hand free leaves a target in reach of that hand off-guard until your next turn.
cf-feat-snowdrift-spell = Snowdrift Spell
cf-feat-snowdrift-spell-desc = Requires storm order. Costs 1 action. If your next spell has the air, water or cold trait and not fire, the ground under and around the first creature it affects fills with snow, difficult terrain for 6 seconds. Clearing the snow by hand, and fire melting it: TBA
cf-feat-solid-lead = Solid Lead
cf-feat-solid-lead-desc = Keep a lead for the day. Investigations do not exist: TBA
cf-feat-songof-glorious-invocation = Song of Glorious Invocation
cf-feat-songof-glorious-invocation-desc = Requires Rune-Singer. Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-songof-strength = Song of Strength
cf-feat-songof-strength-desc = Requires warrior muse. A composition: for a minute, you and allies within 60 feet gain +1 status to Athletics and to the DC against Shove, Trip, Disarm, Grapple and Reposition.
cf-feat-songofthe-soul = Song of the Soul
cf-feat-songofthe-soul-desc = A grave spell. This one: TBA
cf-feat-soothing-vials = Soothing Vials
cf-feat-soothing-vials-desc = Requires chirurgeon research field. Versatile vials are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-spell-protection-array = Spell Protection Array
cf-feat-spell-protection-array-desc = Costs 1 action. A circle that protects against magic: TBA
cf-feat-spellbook-prodigy = Spellbook Prodigy
cf-feat-spellbook-prodigy-desc = Requires trained in Arcana. Better at learning spells: TBA
cf-feat-spirit-familiar-animist = Spirit Familiar (Animist)
cf-feat-spirit-familiar-animist-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-spirit-sheath = Spirit Sheath
cf-feat-spirit-sheath-desc = A hidden place to keep a weapon: TBA
cf-feat-spiritual-expansion-spell = Spiritual Expansion Spell
cf-feat-spiritual-expansion-spell-desc = Costs 1 action. A spellshape. Your next burst, cone or line spell with no duration gets bigger, as Widen Spell.
cf-feat-spiritual-guides = Spiritual Guides
cf-feat-spiritual-guides-desc = Requires spirit instinct. A reaction, automatic, once per long rest: reroll a failed skill check and keep the better result. The rules allow it once an hour.
cf-feat-splinter-faith-champion = Splinter Faith
cf-feat-splinter-faith-champion-desc = Pick any four domains. Your domain feats choose from these instead of your deity's.
cf-feat-splinter-faith-cleric = Splinter Faith
cf-feat-splinter-faith-cleric-desc = Pick any four domains. Your domain feats choose from these instead of your deity's.
cf-feat-split-shot = Split Shot
cf-feat-split-shot-desc = Costs 1 action. A spell attack against two targets: TBA
cf-feat-stand-still = Stand Still
cf-feat-stand-still-desc = Reaction, automatic. Strike an enemy that runs out of your reach. An enemy that walks out and spends 1 action does not set it off. Stopping it on a critical hit: TBA
cf-feat-starlit-eyes = Starlit Eyes
cf-feat-starlit-eyes-desc = Requires starlit span hybrid study. Easier flat checks at range: TBA
cf-feat-steady-spellcasting-magus = Steady Spellcasting (Magus)
cf-feat-steady-spellcasting-magus-desc = Nothing can disrupt a spell yet: TBA
cf-feat-steed-form = Steed Form
cf-feat-steed-form-desc = Ride your eidolon. This one: TBA
cf-feat-steelon-steel = Steel on Steel
cf-feat-steelon-steel-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-storm-born = Storm Born
cf-feat-storm-born-desc = Requires storm order. Weather gives you no penalty to ranged spell attacks or Perception, and does not conceal your spell targets. Weather does none of that to anyone yet: TBA
cf-feat-strategic-assessment = Strategic Assessment
cf-feat-strategic-assessment-desc = Learn a foe's weakness when your stored roll hits: TBA
cf-feat-strikers-scroll = Striker's Scroll
cf-feat-strikers-scroll-desc = Requires Spellstrike. No scrolls exist yet: TBA
cf-feat-strong-arm = Strong Arm
cf-feat-strong-arm-desc = Thrown weapons have a range increment 10 feet longer.
cf-feat-studentof-water = Student of Water
cf-feat-studentof-water-desc = Fighting underwater. Water is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-studentofthe-staff = Student of the Staff
cf-feat-studentofthe-staff-desc = Requires twisting tree hybrid study. A critical hit with a staff knocks the target 10 feet away, as a club's critical specialization. Deadly d6 on the staff in Arcane Cascade, and property runes in a magic staff: TBA
cf-feat-stumbling-stance = Stumbling Stance
cf-feat-stumbling-stance-desc = Costs 1 action. Requires trained in Deception. Your only Strikes are 1d8 bludgeoning stumbling swings. +1 circumstance to Deception, which is your Feint. The opening when you are hit: TBA
cf-feat-stunning-blows = Stunning Blows
cf-feat-stunning-blows-desc = When Flurry of Blows hurts its target, the target rolls Fortitude against your class DC or is stunned 1, stunned 3 on a critical failure. Stunned is that many actions lost at once.
cf-feat-sudden-charge-barbarian = Sudden Charge
cf-feat-sudden-charge-barbarian-desc = Stride into reach and Strike. Costs 2 actions.
cf-feat-sudden-charge-fighter = Sudden Charge
cf-feat-sudden-charge-fighter-desc = Stride into reach and Strike. Costs 2 actions.
cf-feat-supernatural-senses = Supernatural Senses
cf-feat-supernatural-senses-desc = Requires Acute Scent or scent. While raging, the flat check to target a concealed creature is DC 3, and DC 9 for a hidden one.
cf-feat-swaggering-initiative = Swaggering Initiative
cf-feat-swaggering-initiative-desc = Free action. Real time has no initiative: TBA
cf-feat-swan-dive = Swan Dive
cf-feat-swan-dive-desc = Costs 1 action. Dive into water and swim. Water is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-swipe-barbarian = Swipe
cf-feat-swipe-barbarian-desc = Costs 2 actions. A Strike at your target and at an enemy beside it that is within your reach, at the same penalty. It counts as two attacks. Each target gets its own attack and damage roll, where the rules roll once for both.
cf-feat-swipe-fighter = Swipe
cf-feat-swipe-fighter-desc = Costs 2 actions. A Strike at your target and at an enemy beside it that is within your reach, at the same penalty. It counts as two attacks. Each target gets its own attack and damage roll, where the rules roll once for both.
cf-feat-swordand-pistol = Sword and Pistol
cf-feat-swordand-pistol-desc = Mix a one-handed ranged weapon with a melee weapon: TBA
cf-feat-sympathetic-strike = Sympathetic Strike
cf-feat-sympathetic-strike-desc = Requires Witch's Armaments. Costs 1 action, once every 6 seconds. An unarmed Strike. On a hit the target takes -1 circumstance to saves against hexes for 6 seconds, or -2 on a critical hit.
cf-feat-tactical-expansion = Tactical Expansion
cf-feat-tactical-expansion-desc = A folio and swapping tactics are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-takedown-expert = Takedown Expert
cf-feat-takedown-expert-desc = A stored Devise a Stratagem roll can also use Intelligence, and Strategic Strike's damage, with a one-handed weapon of the club group. Nonlethal Strikes without the penalty: TBA
cf-feat-talisman-esoterica = Talisman Esoterica
cf-feat-talisman-esoterica-desc = Temporary talismans. Talismans are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-tamper = Tamper
cf-feat-tamper-desc = Costs 1 action. Sabotage a foe's weapon or armor: TBA
cf-feat-tandem-movement = Tandem Movement
cf-feat-tandem-movement-desc = Costs 1 action. You and your eidolon each get +10 feet Speed for 3 seconds.
cf-feat-tapinto-blood = Tap into Blood
cf-feat-tapinto-blood-desc = Costs 1 action. Blood magic is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-taunting-strike = Taunting Strike
cf-feat-taunting-strike-desc = Costs 1 action. A melee Strike that Taunts the target, hit or miss.
cf-feat-tenacious-toxins = Tenacious Toxins
cf-feat-tenacious-toxins-desc = Your poisons last longer. Poisons are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-terrifying-invocation = Terrifying Invocation
cf-feat-terrifying-invocation-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-thats-odd = That's Odd
cf-feat-thats-odd-desc = Notice something strange in each new place. That needs a game master: TBA
cf-feat-the-hallowed-dead = The Hallowed Dead
cf-feat-the-hallowed-dead-desc = Holy thralls. This one: TBA
cf-feat-the-harder-they-fall = The Harder They Fall
cf-feat-the-harder-they-fall-desc = More damage against prone foes: TBA
cf-feat-the-unholy-dead = The Unholy Dead
cf-feat-the-unholy-dead-desc = Unholy thralls. This one: TBA
cf-feat-thoughtform-summoning = Thoughtform Summoning
cf-feat-thoughtform-summoning-desc = A creature you summon is a thing of thought: it resists physical damage by half its level and has weakness 5 to force and mental damage. Passing through enemies needs nothing here, since creatures do not block each other.
cf-feat-thousand-visions = Thousand Visions
cf-feat-thousand-visions-desc = Free action. Your curse sharpens your senses: TBA
cf-feat-throughthe-needles-eye = Through the Needle's Eye
cf-feat-throughthe-needles-eye-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-tiger-stance = Tiger Stance
cf-feat-tiger-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. Your fists become 1d8 slashing tiger claw attacks (agile, finesse, nonlethal). A critical hit that deals damage adds 1d4 persistent bleed. The 10-foot Step: TBA
cf-feat-topple-the-titans = Topple The Titans
cf-feat-topple-the-titans-desc = Costs 1 action. Trip is not an action here: TBA
cf-feat-tranceof-celerity = Trance of Celerity
cf-feat-tranceof-celerity-desc = Costs 1 action. +5 feet status bonus to Speed for a minute. The increase with your curse: TBA
cf-feat-transpose-etching = Transpose Etching
cf-feat-transpose-etching-desc = Costs 1 action. This one: TBA
cf-feat-trap-finder-investigator = Trap Finder
cf-feat-trap-finder-investigator-desc = +1 circumstance bonus to Perception to notice traps, to AC against their attacks and to saves against them. Everyone here gets a check to notice a trap on coming near it, so there is nothing more to give for finding one without searching. The larger bonus at master, and disabling traps that need master: TBA
cf-feat-trap-finder-rogue = Trap Finder
cf-feat-trap-finder-rogue-desc = +1 circumstance bonus to Perception to notice traps, to AC against their attacks and to saves against them. Everyone here gets a check to notice a trap on coming near it, so there is nothing more to give for finding one without searching. The larger bonus at master, and disabling traps that need master: TBA
cf-feat-tributary-circulation = Tributary Circulation
cf-feat-tributary-circulation-desc = Costs 1 action. +2 circumstance bonus to Will saves and to saves against poison for 6 seconds. The two-action version: TBA
cf-feat-triple-time = Triple Time
cf-feat-triple-time-desc = A composition: for a minute, you and allies within 60 feet gain +10 feet status to Speed.
cf-feat-tumble-behind-rogue = Tumble Behind (Rogue)
cf-feat-tumble-behind-rogue-desc = Automatic. When you Tumble Through an enemy by running into it, it is off-guard to you afterwards.
cf-feat-tumble-behind-swashbuckler = Tumble Behind (Swashbuckler)
cf-feat-tumble-behind-swashbuckler-desc = Automatic. When you Tumble Through an enemy by running into it, it is off-guard to you afterwards.
cf-feat-turn-away-misfortune = Turn Away Misfortune
cf-feat-turn-away-misfortune-desc = Reaction. Cancel a misfortune effect. There is no trigger for it yet: TBA
cf-feat-twin-distraction = Twin Distraction
cf-feat-twin-distraction-desc = Requires Twin Feint. When both Twin Feint Strikes hit, the target makes a Will save against your class DC or is stupefied 1 for 6 seconds.
cf-feat-twin-feint = Twin Feint
cf-feat-twin-feint-desc = Right-click one creature with a melee weapon in each hand: one Strike with each. The target is off-guard against the second. Costs 2 actions.
cf-feat-twin-parry-fighter = Twin Parry
cf-feat-twin-parry-fighter-desc = Costs 1 action. With a melee weapon in each hand, +1 circumstance bonus to AC for 6 seconds. The +2 against a parry trait weapon: TBA
cf-feat-twin-parry-ranger = Twin Parry
cf-feat-twin-parry-ranger-desc = Costs 1 action. With a melee weapon in each hand, +1 circumstance bonus to AC for 6 seconds. The +2 against a parry trait weapon: TBA
cf-feat-twin-stars = Twin Stars
cf-feat-twin-stars-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-twin-takedown = Twin Takedown
cf-feat-twin-takedown-desc = Costs 1 action, a flourish. Strike your prey once with the weapon in each hand. Combining the damage against resistances: TBA
cf-feat-twirling-throw = Twirling Throw
cf-feat-twirling-throw-desc = Requires Flying Blade. Costs 1 action. A thrown weapon that comes back: TBA
cf-feat-twisting-petal-stance = Twisting Petal Stance
cf-feat-twisting-petal-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. Requires trained in Deception. Your fists become 1d6 slashing gale blossom strikes. +1 circumstance to your Athletics maneuvers and to Deception, and +2 to your DC against maneuvers. The rules limit these to Shove and Feint.
cf-feat-unbalancing-blow = Unbalancing Blow
cf-feat-unbalancing-blow-desc = Requires the thief racket. A critical hit that deals damage leaves the target off-guard to you for a round.
cf-feat-unbalancing-finisher = Unbalancing Finisher
cf-feat-unbalancing-finisher-desc = Costs 1 action and your panache. A melee finisher. If it deals damage, the target is off-guard for 6 seconds. Use your weapon in hand (Z) to switch to it, and Alt+Z to perform it.
cf-feat-undead-creator = Undead Creator
cf-feat-undead-creator-desc = Create permanent undead. Rituals are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-undead-familiar = Undead Familiar
cf-feat-undead-familiar-desc = A familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you and does not fight. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-underhanded-assault = Underhanded Assault
cf-feat-underhanded-assault-desc = Requires trained in Stealth. Costs 2 actions. Sneak up to a foe beside an ally and Strike it. It needs a path to follow: TBA
cf-feat-underworld-investigator = Underworld Investigator
cf-feat-underworld-investigator-desc = Underworld Lore and a bonus while on a case. Investigations do not exist: TBA
cf-feat-unfetter-eidolon = Unfetter Eidolon
cf-feat-unfetter-eidolon-desc = A link spell. This one: TBA
cf-feat-unimpeded-step = Unimpeded Step
cf-feat-unimpeded-step-desc = Requires liberation cause. The ally's Step ignores difficult terrain. That Step is not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-unsteadying-strike = Unsteadying Strike
cf-feat-unsteadying-strike-desc = Costs 1 action. A melee Strike. If it hits, the target takes -2 circumstance to its DCs against being Shoved, Grappled, Repositioned or Disarmed for 6 seconds.
cf-feat-untamed-form = Untamed Form
cf-feat-untamed-form-desc = Requires untamed order. You learn Untamed Form, a focus spell. You become a pest for 10 minutes, which cannot attack, or from level 3 an ape, bear, bull, canine, cat or deer for a minute. Your own attack modifier gets +2 status in the form when you use it. Dismiss Form ends it early.
cf-feat-uplifting-overture = Uplifting Overture
cf-feat-uplifting-overture-desc = Requires maestro muse. TBA
cf-feat-vampiric-spell = Vampiric Spell
cf-feat-vampiric-spell-desc = Spellshape. The next spell you cast that deals damage gives you temporary Hit Points equal to half the most damage it dealt one creature, for a minute: TBA
cf-feat-variable-core = Variable Core
cf-feat-variable-core-desc = Change what your innovation explodes with. This option: TBA
cf-feat-verdant-weapon = Verdant Weapon
cf-feat-verdant-weapon-desc = You get a verdant seed. Right-click it in your hand to grow it into a staff, a spear or a sling for 1 action, and right-click the weapon to turn it back. Runes on the weapon do not survive the change: TBA
cf-feat-versatile-font = Versatile Font
cf-feat-versatile-font-desc = Requires harmful font or healing font and a deity that allows both. Here a deity that allows both fonts already gives its followers Heal and Harm, so this feat adds nothing. Picking one font at level 1, which this feat would lift: TBA
cf-feat-versatile-performance = Versatile Performance
cf-feat-versatile-performance-desc = Requires polymath muse. You Demoralize with Performance when it is better than Intimidation. Make an Impression and Impersonate with Performance, and meeting feat prerequisites with it: TBA
cf-feat-versatile-signature = Versatile Signature
cf-feat-versatile-signature-desc = Requires polymath muse. TBA
cf-feat-vibration-sense = Vibration Sense
cf-feat-vibration-sense-desc = Your eidolon gains tremorsense. This one: TBA
cf-feat-vicious-swing = Vicious Swing
cf-feat-vicious-swing-desc = Right-click one creature for a Strike with one extra damage die, two at 10th level and three at 18th. Counts as two attacks. Costs 2 actions. Flourish.
cf-feat-vicious-vengeance = Vicious Vengeance
cf-feat-vicious-vengeance-desc = Requires iniquity cause. Destructive Vengeance deals 1 more spirit damage to the enemy, or 2 more from level 5.
cf-feat-violent-unleash = Violent Unleash
cf-feat-violent-unleash-desc = Costs 1 action. A force blast as you Unleash your Psyche: TBA
cf-feat-void-siphon-necromancer = Void Siphon (Necromancer)
cf-feat-void-siphon-necromancer-desc = Reaction. Absorb void damage. Reactions do not read damage types yet: TBA
cf-feat-vowof-mortal-defiance = Vow of Mortal Defiance
cf-feat-vowof-mortal-defiance-desc = Costs 1 action. Swear off the gods: TBA
cf-feat-walkthe-wilds = Walk the Wilds
cf-feat-walkthe-wilds-desc = Add animal form to your apparition spells. This one: TBA
cf-feat-warning-shot = Warning Shot
cf-feat-warning-shot-desc = Requires trained in Intimidation. Costs 1 action. Demoralize with a gunshot. TBA
cf-feat-warp-space = Warp Space
cf-feat-warp-space-desc = Amps from feats are not built yet: TBA
cf-feat-warpriests-armor = Warpriest's Armor
cf-feat-warpriests-armor-desc = You are trained in heavy armor. Later armor proficiency applying to it too: TBA
cf-feat-waterfowl-stance = Waterfowl Stance
cf-feat-waterfowl-stance-desc = Requires Monastic Weaponry. Costs 1 action. Weapons do not have the monk trait yet: TBA
cf-feat-weightof-guilt = Weight of Guilt
cf-feat-weightof-guilt-desc = Requires redemption cause. Glimpse of Redemption makes the enemy stupefied 2 for 6 seconds instead of enfeebled 2. It always does, where the rules let you choose each time.
cf-feat-well-versed = Well-Versed
cf-feat-well-versed-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against auditory, illusion, linguistic, sonic and visual effects.
cf-feat-whispersof-weakness = Whispers of Weakness
cf-feat-whispersof-weakness-desc = Costs 1 action. Cursebound. Recall Knowledge about a creature within 60 feet at no cost, and get +2 status to attack rolls for 6 seconds. The rules tell you its weaknesses with no check.
cf-feat-widen-spell-druid = Widen Spell
cf-feat-widen-spell-druid-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next burst of at least 10 feet, cone or line with no duration gets bigger: bursts by 5 feet, cones and lines by 5 feet up to 15 long, otherwise 10. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-widen-spell-oracle = Widen Spell
cf-feat-widen-spell-oracle-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next burst of at least 10 feet, cone or line with no duration gets bigger: bursts by 5 feet, cones and lines by 5 feet up to 15 long, otherwise 10. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-widen-spell-sorcerer = Widen Spell
cf-feat-widen-spell-sorcerer-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next burst of at least 10 feet, cone or line with no duration gets bigger: bursts by 5 feet, cones and lines by 5 feet up to 15 long, otherwise 10. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-widen-spell-witch = Widen Spell
cf-feat-widen-spell-witch-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next burst of at least 10 feet, cone or line with no duration gets bigger: bursts by 5 feet, cones and lines by 5 feet up to 15 long, otherwise 10. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-widen-spell-wizard = Widen Spell
cf-feat-widen-spell-wizard-desc = Costs 1 action. Your next burst of at least 10 feet, cone or line with no duration gets bigger: bursts by 5 feet, cones and lines by 5 feet up to 15 long, otherwise 10. Lost if you spend an action on anything else first.
cf-feat-widespread-fascination = Widespread Fascination
cf-feat-widespread-fascination-desc = A second grave spell. This one: TBA
cf-feat-witchs-armaments = Witch's Armaments
cf-feat-witchs-armaments-desc = Choose an unarmed attack. Eldritch nails: 1d6 slashing, agile. Iron teeth: 1d8 piercing. Living hair: 1d4 bludgeoning, agile, finesse. The hair's disarm and trip traits: TBA
cf-feat-wolf-stance = Wolf Stance
cf-feat-wolf-stance-desc = Costs 1 action, needs no armor. Your fists become 1d8 piercing wolf jaw attacks with agile, backstabber and finesse. Trip while flanking: TBA
cf-feat-wolfin-sheeps-clothing = Wolf in Sheep's Clothing
cf-feat-wolfin-sheeps-clothing-desc = Requires Trained in Deception. TBA
cf-feat-wounded-rage = Wounded Rage
cf-feat-wounded-rage-desc = Reaction, automatic. When you take damage and are able to rage, you enter a rage.
cf-feat-writing-onthe-wall = Writing On the Wall
cf-feat-writing-onthe-wall-desc = This one: TBA
cf-feat-wukong-extension = Wukong Extension
cf-feat-wukong-extension-desc = Requires weapon innovation. Costs 1 action. This option: TBA
cf-feat-youre-next-rogue = You're Next
cf-feat-youre-next-rogue-desc = Reaction. When you drop a creature to 0 HP, Demoralize another foe within 30 feet. +2 circumstance bonus.
cf-feat-youre-next-swashbuckler = You're Next
cf-feat-youre-next-swashbuckler-desc = Reaction. When you drop a creature to 0 HP, Demoralize another foe within 30 feet. +2 circumstance bonus.
cf-feat-zoophonic-communication = Zoophonic Communication
cf-feat-zoophonic-communication-desc = Requires zoophonia muse. TBA
cf-feat-zoophonic-composition = Zoophonic Composition
cf-feat-zoophonic-composition-desc = Requires zoophonia muse. Free action. Speak to animals through a composition: TBA
